---
import DocLayout from '../../layouts/DocLayout.astro';
---

<DocLayout title="Forms" description="Form components in the Farn design system — inputs, selects, textareas, and form layout patterns">
  <h1>Forms</h1>
  <p>
    Form element styles ship as bare element selectors — no extra classes required on
    <code>input</code>, <code>textarea</code>, or <code>select</code>. All styles consume
    Tier-3 <code>--input-*</code> tokens so the full form palette can be rethemed in one
    place without touching semantic tokens.
  </p>

  <!-- ── Form elements ────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

  <h2 id="form-elements">Form elements <span class="badge badge-published">stable</span></h2>
  <p>
    Include <code>farn-components.css</code> — every <code>input</code>, <code>textarea</code>,
    and <code>select</code> is styled automatically. Use <code>.form-field</code> to group a
    label with its control and optional hint text.
  </p>

  <div class="form-demo demo-surface" role="group" aria-label="Form element examples">
    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="demo-text">Text input</label>
      <input type="text" id="demo-text" placeholder="Placeholder text" />
    </div>
    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="demo-select">Select</label>
      <select id="demo-select">
        <option value="">Choose an option</option>
        <option value="fern">Fern</option>
        <option value="forest">Forest</option>
        <option value="deepwater">Deepwater</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="demo-textarea">Textarea</label>
      <textarea id="demo-textarea" placeholder="Longer text…"></textarea>
    </div>
    <div class="form-field">
      <label>
        <input type="checkbox" /> Remember me
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>States</h3>
  <p>Hover darkens to <code>--input-bg-active</code>. Focus adds a coloured border and glow ring via <code>--input-focus-shadow</code>. Error via <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> (preferred — screen readers announce it) or the <code>.form-field--error</code> wrapper, which also colours the label and hint. Disabled reduces opacity via <code>--input-disabled-opacity</code> and suppresses pointer events.</p>
  <div class="form-demo demo-surface" role="group" aria-label="Form input state examples">
    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="state-default">Default</label>
      <input type="text" id="state-default" placeholder="Idle" />
    </div>
    <div class="form-field form-field--error">
      <label for="state-error">Error</label>
      <input type="text" id="state-error" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="state-error-hint" value="bad@" />
      <span class="form-hint" id="state-error-hint">Invalid value.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="state-disabled">Disabled</label>
      <input type="text" id="state-disabled" value="Cannot edit" disabled />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Wrapper + hint</h3>
  <p><code>.form-field</code> stacks label, control, and optional hint text with consistent spacing. <code>.form-hint</code> renders helper or error text below the control in a smaller, secondary colour.</p>
  <div class="form-demo demo-surface" role="group" aria-label="Form field wrapper and hint text examples">
    <div class="form-field">
      <label for="wrapper-name">Username</label>
      <input type="text" id="wrapper-name" placeholder="jane_smith" />
      <span class="form-hint">3–24 characters, letters and underscores only.</span>
    </div>
    <div class="form-field form-field--error">
      <label for="wrapper-email">Email</label>
      <input type="email" id="wrapper-email" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="wrapper-email-hint" value="not-an-email" />
      <span class="form-hint" id="wrapper-email-hint">Enter a valid email address.</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="accordion">
    <details>
      <summary>Full reference — Form elements</summary>
      <div class="accordion-panel">

        <h3>Anatomy</h3>
        <pre><code>&lt;!-- Minimal — element selector handles all styling --&gt;
&lt;input type="text" placeholder="…" /&gt;

&lt;!-- With label --&gt;
&lt;label for="x"&gt;Label&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;input type="text" id="x" /&gt;

&lt;!-- Full wrapper pattern --&gt;
&lt;div class="form-field"&gt;
  &lt;label for="name"&gt;Name&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" id="name" placeholder="Jane Smith" /&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;!-- With hint text --&gt;
&lt;div class="form-field"&gt;
  &lt;label for="username"&gt;Username&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input type="text" id="username" /&gt;
  &lt;span class="form-hint"&gt;3–24 characters, letters and underscores only.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;!-- Error via ARIA attribute --&gt;
&lt;input type="email" aria-invalid="true" value="bad@" /&gt;

&lt;!-- Error via wrapper — colours label and hint too; aria-describedby links hint to input --&gt;
&lt;div class="form-field form-field--error"&gt;
  &lt;label for="email"&gt;Email&lt;/label&gt;
  &lt;input type="email" id="email" aria-invalid="true"
         aria-describedby="email-hint" value="bad@" /&gt;
  &lt;span class="form-hint" id="email-hint"&gt;Enter a valid email address.&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;!-- Disabled --&gt;
&lt;input type="text" disabled value="Cannot edit" /&gt;</code></pre>

        <h3>Token reference</h3>
        <p>All <code>--input-*</code> tokens are defined in <code>tokens/components.css</code>.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Default</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>--input-radius</code></td><td><code>var(--radius-md)</code></td><td>Border radius for all form controls</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-bg</code></td><td><code>var(--color-bg-panel)</code></td><td>Idle background</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-bg-active</code></td><td><code>var(--color-bg-inset)</code></td><td>Hover and focus background</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-border</code></td><td><code>transparent</code></td><td>Idle border colour (invisible by default)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-border-focus</code></td><td><code>var(--color-accent)</code></td><td>Focus border colour</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-border-error</code></td><td><code>var(--color-error)</code></td><td>Error border colour</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-focus-shadow</code></td><td><code>0 0 0 3px color-mix(…)</code></td><td>Focus glow ring</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-text</code></td><td><code>var(--color-text)</code></td><td>Input text colour</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-placeholder</code></td><td><code>var(--color-text-tertiary)</code></td><td>Placeholder text colour</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--input-disabled-opacity</code></td><td><code>0.4</code></td><td>Opacity applied to disabled controls</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <h3>Overriding tokens</h3>
        <pre><code>/* Tighter radius for a dense data-entry panel */
.data-panel &#123;
  --input-radius: var(--radius-sm);
&#125;

/* Visible idle border in a flat section */
.flat-form &#123;
  --input-bg:     transparent;
  --input-border: var(--color-border);
&#125;</code></pre>

      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

</DocLayout>

<style>
  .form-demo {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    /* override .demo-surface's --space-md for section-level breathing room */
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    max-width: var(--width-prose);
  }
</style>
